BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Congregation Shomrei Emunah
UID:TU2006148638
DTSTAMP:20260926T004146Z
SUMMARY:Midday MeetUp - Blueberries\, New Jersey’s Wonder Fruit
DESCRIPTION:**Midday MeetUp - Blueberries\, New Jersey’s Wonder Fruit**  
  \nA monthly gathering to make connections and learn together.  \n11:45am 
 Catered Lunch (free)  \n12:30pm Featured Program   \n  \nSpeaker: Food his
 torian\, Judith Krall-Russo  \n  \nThe cultivated blueberry has its roots 
 in the Pinelands of New Jersey. Elizabeth White along with Dr. Fredrick Co
 ville\, proved that the “swamp huckleberry” could be cultivated. Learn
  the history of this fascinating berry and the contributions Elizabeth Whi
 te of Whitesbog made to their cultivation. Today the blueberry is touted a
 s the wonder fruit with a host of healthful benefits. Learn about the hist
 ory\, health benefits and a variety of ways to prepare and savor these ber
 ries.  \n  \n**Cost:** FREE or Suggested Donation of $10 per person to off
 set costs. (Bill My Account is only open to Shomrei Members)  \n  \n**RSVP
 :** Required so we know how much food to buy.  \nhttps://shomrei.easyshul.
 com/events/6967e4b6368f110026c0c460  \n  \n**\\***Members &amp\; PreSchool
  Families should use their fob to access the building.   \n  \nFull_Season
 _Schedule_for_Midday_MeetUps: https://shomrei.org/calendar/midday-meetup-c
 alendar  \n  \n**Questions?** Contact June Zimmerman\,   \nVP for Programm
 ing  \njzimmerman@shomrei.org  \n  \n\\#middaymeetup\n\n
LOCATION:Social Hall
CATEGORIES:Events
CLASS:PUBLIC
TRANSP:OPAQUE
SEQUENCE:0
