X-SOURCE:Congregation Shomrei Emunah
UID:TU2131910341
DTSTAMP:20260926T004146Z
SUMMARY:Selichot - Service\, Dinner\, Music!
DESCRIPTION:Start the High Holidays with joy\, music and community! Join us
  for a lively evening packed with delicious food\, soulful singing and swe
 et treats. Connect with the Shomrei community over dinner and sing High Ho
 liday melodies. Unwind with dessert and smooth sounds from our jazz band. 
 It’s a celebration you won’t want to miss!\n\n**RSVP Required for Dinn
 er and Reception** **http://shomrei.org/jazz**: http://shomrei.org/jazz\n\
 nFree or Suggested Donation:  \n$20 per adult\, $10 per child over 12\, $3
 6 per family\n\n**------------------------------  \nAdults and Kids 8+ (Yo
 unger Kids/Scroll Down)**  \n6:30 Welcome   \n6:45 Dinner (Middle Eastern 
 dairy dinner)  \n8:00 Havdalah and Selichot Service  \n9:00 Dessert and Ja
 zz Reception\n\nAs Shabbat comes to a close\, children and adults will com
 e together to recite Havdalah prayers. We are looking forward to having ou
 r children who are 8 yrs old and up help lead the havdalah candle lighting
  ceremony while reciting prayers with Rabbi Julie.\n\nParticipatory\, musi
 c-filled service led by Rabbi Julie\, Talia Lakritz\, Suzanna Grobman\, De
 bra Caplan and accompanied by Oren Neiman and his jazz ensemble.\n\nThe pa
 rty continues with a dessert reception. Live music will be provided by the
  jazz ensemble.\n\n**Livestream:** http://shomrei.org/live\n\n**----------
 --------------------**\n\n**Kids 7 and Younger**  \n6:30 Little Kids' Dinn
 er   \n7:00 Free Play  \n7:30 Selichot Inspired Art Activity  \n8:00 Child
 ren welcome to stay in childcare\, or join Selichot service\n\n**---------
 ---------------------**\n\n**Have questions? Want to Help out? Contact:** 
 Shomrei Office  \noffice@shomrei.org  \n(973) 746-5031\n\n**What is Selich
 ot?**  \nThe Hebrew word selichah means “forgiveness.” The plural form
  of the word selichah is selichot\, a word traditionally used to refer to 
 additional prayers for forgiveness recited during the month of Elul (throu
 gh Yom Kippur). We gather together on the Saturday night before Rosh Hasha
 nah to meditate on the capacity for forgiveness and on its power. In joini
 ng together\, we help each other pray for that blessing – to give it and
  to receive it.\n\n
LOCATION:Social Hall\, Gallery\, [#]holiday:rosh_hashanah\, ~Extra Parking:
  73 & 77 Park St.\, Livestream
CATEGORIES:Events
CLASS:PUBLIC
TRANSP:OPAQUE
SEQUENCE:0
